EXAM_DATA.papers["2014-english-one"] = {"id":"2014-english-one","year":2014,"label":"2014 英语一","era":"modern","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2014-english-one/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"estimated","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"As many people hit middle age, they often start to notice that their memory and mental clarity are not what they used to be. We suddenly can't remember   {{1}}   we put the keys just a moment ago, or an old acquaintance's name, or the name of an old band we used to love. As the brain   {{2}}   , we refer to these occurrences as \"senior moments.\"   {{3}}   seemingly innocent, this loss of mental focus can potentially have a(n)   {{4}}   impact on our professional, social, and personal   {{5}}   ."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"Neuroscientists, experts who study the nervous system, are increasingly showing that there's actually a lot that can be done. It   {{6}}   out that the brain needs exercise in much the same way our muscles do, and the right mental   {{7}}   can significantly improve our basic cognitive   {{8}}   . Thinking is essentially a   {{9}}   of making connections in the brain. To a certain extent, our ability to   {{10}}   in making the connections that drive intelligence is inherited.   {{11}}   , because these connections are made through effort and practice, scientists believe that intelligence can expand and fluctuate   {{12}}   mental effort."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"Now, a new Web-based company has taken it a step   {{13}}   and developed the first \"brain training program\" designed to actually help people improve and regain their mental   {{14}}   ."},{"id":"p-section1-4","text":"The Web-based program   {{15}}   you to systematically improve your memory and attention skills. The program keeps   {{16}}   of your progress and provides detailed feedback   {{17}}   your performance and improvement. Most importantly, it   {{18}}   modifies and enhances the games you play to   {{19}}   on the strengths you are developing – much like a(n)   {{20}}   exercise routine requires you to increase resistance and vary your muscle use."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"when"},{"key":"C","text":"why"},{"key":"D","text":"where"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"语法形态","stemZh":"1.","reason":"并列项给出对照——地点+人名+乐队名 本句并列三件忘掉的事：we put the keys just a moment ago, or an old acquaintance's name, or the name of an old band we used to love——后两件是名字（人、乐队），第一件应是钥匙的去向，即 put 的地点，故空格指向 where。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"that 只引导陈述事实的宾语从句，本句缺的是 put 的地点状语，that 无地点指向，且与后并列项 an old acquaintance's name（缺名字）的语义对照对不上，排除。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"句内已有时间状语 just a moment ago，再填 when 会与之冲突；中年人忘的也通常不是放钥匙的时间，而是放在哪儿。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"why 指向放钥匙的原因，但放钥匙这种动作无所谓原因，且与并列项语义范畴（人名、乐队名）也不在同一维度，排除。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"where 引出地点状语，正好补全 put the keys 的去向，与并列的人名、乐队名同属典型记忆失误，契合 senior moments 的具象画面。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fades"},{"key":"B","text":"improves"},{"key":"C","text":"collapses"},{"key":"D","text":"recovers"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"整段在描述记忆衰退 上文 their memory and mental clarity are not what they used to be 与下文 senior moments 都指向脑力下滑，空所在句 As the brain __(2)__ 是引出 senior moments 这一称呼的原因状语，必然是负向变化；同时这种下滑属正常老化、缓慢温和，不是灾难。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"fades 意为渐渐衰退/褪色，强度温和、过程渐进，与中年人偶发性 senior moments 的画面完全吻合，是对大脑功能自然老化的最佳描述。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"improves 是正向改善，与上文 memory and mental clarity are not what they used to be 的负面定调完全相反，直接出局。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"collapses 意为崩溃、垮掉，强度过强，等同于丧失认知功能；但下文只是说偶尔忘事，远未到崩溃地步，属于程度上的过度推断。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"recovers 表恢复/痊愈，方向上是正向改善，与全段衰退基调不合，且大脑若在恢复也就不会出现 senior moments，逻辑自相矛盾。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Unless"},{"key":"B","text":"While"},{"key":"C","text":"Once"},{"key":"D","text":"If"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"3.","reason":"前正后负的让步对照 从句 seemingly innocent 是正向（看起来没什么大不了），主句 this loss of mental focus can potentially have a(n) __(4)__ impact on our professional, social, and personal 是负向（其实有不良影响），明显是 让步—转折 的对照关系。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Unless 表 除非……否则，会导出 除非看起来无害、否则会有不良影响 的怪逻辑，与上下文不符，排除。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"While 在句首引导让步状语从句，意为 尽管看似无害，seemingly innocent 与主句 can potentially have a(n) __(4)__ impact 一正一负，对照完美。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Once 表 一旦……就，但 看似无害 不是一个会触发后果的条件事件，前后分句根本不构成 一旦 X 就 Y 的链条。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"If 只表条件假设，无让步含义；若用 If，主句应是 如果看似无害则会有影响 的奇怪条件，逻辑不通；且 If 也漏掉了 看似 与 实际 的对照味道，让步力度不够。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"damaging"},{"key":"B","text":"limited"},{"key":"C","text":"uneven"},{"key":"D","text":"obscure"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"前句 seemingly innocent 反衬出后文的有害 seemingly innocent 表层无害，让步之后必然要揭示 实质有害，且原文用 can potentially have a(n) __(4)__ impact on our professional, social, and personal 三个维度展开，可见影响的范围大、性质坏，需要一个显著负面的形容词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"damaging 直接表 有害的，与 seemingly innocent 构成强烈对照，又能合理统辖 professional, social, and personal 三大维度，是唯一同时满足方向与强度的选项。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"limited 意为 有限的，但作者意在强调 别小看它，影响其实很广，limited 反而把影响往小了说，与让步反差的目的相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"uneven 意为 不均匀的，描述的是分布问题；但作者讲的是影响是否严重、是否负面，不是分布是否均匀，维度错位。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"obscure 意为 模糊、晦涩的，但作者要说的是影响 实实在在地存在 且涉及三大领域，不是 难以察觉。词义方向与作者立场冲突。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"relationship"},{"key":"B","text":"environment"},{"key":"C","text":"wellbeing"},{"key":"D","text":"outlook"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"5.","reason":"三类属性词限定共指的生活总称 professional, social, and personal 三词是同级并列的生活领域；要找一个能被这三者共同修饰的、表 整体生活状态 的词。结合上句话题 memory and mental clarity 的影响范围，应是涉及个人生活整体福祉的词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"relationship 主要指人际关系，professional relationship 可指工作关系，但单数形式与 professional, social, and personal 三项并列时显得偏窄，且 personal relationship 通常是 私人感情，含义偏狭。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"environment 指环境，关注外部场景而非主体感受；但记忆衰退是 个人主观体验问题，影响的是个人 状态而不是 周遭环境，搭配方向偏了。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"wellbeing 意为整体的健康、福祉，可同时被职业、社交、个人三个属性修饰，正好涵盖记忆衰退波及的方方面面，最贴合作者意图。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"outlook 指 前景/看法，更偏未来展望或个人态度，不是被记忆衰退直接 影响 的生活领域；与 professional, social, and personal 三方面 受冲击 的语义结构不匹配。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"figures"},{"key":"B","text":"finds"},{"key":"C","text":"points"},{"key":"D","text":"turns"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"6.","reason":"It…out that…的固定框架本身就是线索 It __(6)__ out that the brain needs exercise in much the same way our muscles do 中，主句是 It…out that 形式句型，that 之后是事实小句，固定搭配 turn out 在此意为 结果证明、事实表明。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"figures 与 out 联用是 figure out（弄明白）但主语应是人 someone figures out something，不与 It…that 形式主语搭配，框架不对。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"finds + out = find out（查明）也需人作主语，且语法上 It finds out that… 完全不通，框架不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"points + out = point out（指出），常是 someone points out that…，没有 It points out that… 的合法用法，框架错。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"turns + out 与形式主语 It 组合成 It turns out that…（结果发现），是英语高频句型，完美套入 It __(6)__ out that the brain needs exercise 引出下文事实小句。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"responses"},{"key":"B","text":"associations"},{"key":"C","text":"workouts"},{"key":"D","text":"roundabouts"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"7.","reason":"上句 exercise 与肌肉的类比指向 上句 the brain needs exercise in much the same way our muscles do 用 exercise 把大脑和肌肉绑在一起类比，本句继续说 the right mental ___，自然要选一个与 exercise/锻炼 同义的词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"responses 意为反应，强调被动应激，与 锻炼 的主动训练含义脱钩，断了与上句 exercise 的类比线。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"associations 是联想/联结，更接近思维内容本身，不是 提升 cognitive functions 的 训练方式，无法对应 exercise。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"workouts 意为 锻炼/训练，与上句 exercise 是直接同义词，完美承接 大脑—肌肉 类比，mental workouts 也是英语中常见说法（脑力训练）。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"roundabouts 指环形交叉路或迂回方式，与脑力训练无任何语义关联，是干扰性最弱的形近误项。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"genre"},{"key":"B","text":"criterion"},{"key":"C","text":"circumstances"},{"key":"D","text":"functions"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"8.","reason":"improve 与 cognitive 共同限定中心名词 the right mental __(7)__ can significantly improve our basic cognitive __(8)__：句子要表达 提升基本认知能力，可被 improve 且可被 cognitive 修饰的就是 functions（功能）；此外上下文反复出现 memory、Thinking 等具体认知功能，也呼应 functions 一词的复数意味。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"genre 指文艺作品的体裁/流派，本文谈的是认知功能而非艺术分类，话题完全错位。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"criterion 意为标准/准则，标准本身不能被 improve（只会被 raise/lower/refine），动宾不合；且 cognitive criterion 也不是英语习惯表达。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"circumstances 指外部情况/境况，是外部环境概念，与人脑内部的 认知能力 不在一个范畴，与 cognitive 不搭。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"functions 与 cognitive 搭成 cognitive functions（认知功能），是神经科学语境中的高频固定搭配，且 可被 improve、可被 basic 修饰，三层兼容性都满足。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"channel"},{"key":"B","text":"process"},{"key":"C","text":"condition"},{"key":"D","text":"sequence"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"下文持续展开 connections 的形成机理 下文 because these connections are made through effort and practice, scientists believe that intelligence can expand 反复强调 connections 是 在过程中逐步形成的，所以本句要把 thinking 定义为一种 持续的过程。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"channel 指渠道/通路，强调信息流动的路径，但 思维 这里被定义为 建立连接的活动 本身，不是 信息流动的通道，方向不合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"process 表 过程，a process of making connections 表 建立连接的过程，与下文 these connections are made through effort and practice 的动态生成观完全契合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"condition 指条件/状态，是静态描述；但作者把 thinking 视为 不断建立连接 的动态活动，condition 与该动感不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"sequence 强调先后顺序、序列，过于狭隘；思维并不必然是线性序列，且 a sequence of making connections 也不是英语习惯表达。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"persist"},{"key":"B","text":"feature"},{"key":"C","text":"excel"},{"key":"D","text":"believe"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"10.","reason":"drive intelligence 暗示能力强弱、与天赋挂钩 our ability to __(10)__ in making the connections that drive intelligence is inherited 句末 is inherited 说明 这种能力是遗传来的，意思是 在建立这些智力连接方面表现出色的能力是遗传的，关键是 表现出色，所以选 excel。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"persist in 表 坚持做某事，但 坚持力 通常不被视为天生遗传特征；与句末 is inherited 的逻辑也不顺。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"feature 多作及物动词 以……为特色，不与 in doing 搭配，语法上就站不住脚。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"excel in 表 在……方面出色/擅长，与 is inherited 衔接为 在建立连接方面表现出色的能力是遗传的，与下一句 intelligence can expand and fluctuate 也保持智力可塑的对照。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"believe in 表 相信，但 相信建立连接 不构成可遗传的认知能力，语义跑偏。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"However"},{"key":"B","text":"Moreover"},{"key":"C","text":"Otherwise"},{"key":"D","text":"Therefore"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"11.","reason":"前句天赋决定—本句后天可塑，呈反向 上句 our ability to __(10)__ in making the connections that drive intelligence is inherited 是 天赋遗传决定，本句 because these connections are made through effort and practice, scientists believe that intelligence can expand and fluctuate 强调 后天努力可让智力扩展波动，前后呈对照的转折关系。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"However 表转折，正好承接前句 智力是遗传的 与本句 但通过努力可扩展 的反差，是唯一能同时满足 反方向 与 副词形态 的选项。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Moreover 表递进/此外，方向同上句，但前后呈反差，递进会让 天赋决定 与 后天可塑 变成奇怪的并列，逻辑不通。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Otherwise 表 否则、不然，需要一个明示或暗示的条件假设供其否定；前文并无 if 假设，逻辑链断。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Therefore 表 因此，前后是因果同向；但 智力遗传 与 后天可扩展 不是因果而是反差，方向不合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"according to"},{"key":"B","text":"regardless of"},{"key":"C","text":"apart from"},{"key":"D","text":"instead of"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"12.","reason":"上下文反复强调脑力训练能改变智力 全段 these connections are made through effort and practice 与 intelligence can expand and fluctuate 都在强调 智力随努力变化，可见智力变化是 依赖于 脑力投入，应填 according to。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"according to 意为 依据、随着，正合本句 智力随脑力投入而变化 的含义，也与 effort and practice 的因果一致。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"regardless of 表 不顾、不论，意味着智力变化与脑力投入无关；但全段刚说 智力靠努力扩展，方向相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"apart from 表 除……之外，会暗示 除脑力投入外，智力还会因别的扩展，但上下文没有讨论其他因素，逻辑无依据。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"instead of 表 而不是，会让句意变成 智力扩展而不是脑力投入，根本说不通，也与 effort and practice 决定智力变化的论点冲突。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"back"},{"key":"B","text":"further"},{"key":"C","text":"aside"},{"key":"D","text":"around"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"13.","reason":"上文给出理论，本句再进一步推出产品 前面段落 there's actually a lot that can be done 仅提出 大脑可训练 的理论，本句 taken it a step __(13)__ and developed the first \"brain training program\" 紧跟着把理论 推进 到产品落地，逻辑上是 更进一步。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"back = step back（退后一步），逻辑上和上文 推出新产品 的递进完全相反。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"further = take it a step further（更进一步），描述这家公司在科学家的理论基础上 进一步把它做成训练程序，是搭配与语义双合的答案。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"aside 多指 把……放一边，与本句 推出新产品 的积极动作冲突。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"around = step around（绕开），与递进逻辑无关，也不是 take it a step around 的英语习语。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"framework"},{"key":"B","text":"stability"},{"key":"C","text":"flexibility"},{"key":"D","text":"sharpness"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"14.","reason":"第一段 mental clarity 与 senior moments 呼应 第一段 their memory and mental clarity are not what they used to be 与 this loss of mental focus 给出训练要 找回 的东西是 心智的清晰度/敏锐度，与 sharpness（敏锐）正好对应。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"framework 指 框架/结构，与第一段失去的 mental clarity（清晰、敏锐）不对位，不是中年人需要 找回 的东西。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"stability 指稳定性，但第一段未提到 心理不稳；脑训练程序解决的是 反应变慢、记忆变差，而不是 心理稳定 问题。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"flexibility 表灵活度，虽然与脑力训练有点沾边，但第一段失去的是清晰度与专注力，灵活度并非主线，回环对应不上。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"sharpness 意为 敏锐度，与第一段 mental clarity、mental focus 在语义上呼应；脑训练程序要 找回 的正是这种 思维的敏锐度。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"hurries"},{"key":"B","text":"reminds"},{"key":"C","text":"allows"},{"key":"D","text":"forces"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"15.","reason":"推介性段落的友好语气 第四段整段在介绍产品如何帮用户进步，包括 keeps __(16)__ of your progress 与 provides detailed feedback __(17)__ your performance and improvement，整体语气积极友好，是 邀请 而非 强制 用户。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"hurries 表催促，给人 程序在催你 的感觉，与推介性段落的友好语气冲突。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"reminds 表 提醒，多指 提醒做某事；但 systematically improve 是 系统地训练，需要 让你做 而非 提醒做，搭配不准。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"allows 表 让/使你能够，把程序的作用定位为 赋能 用户系统训练，与下文的 追踪进度、反馈表现、动态调整 的辅助角色完全一致。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"forces 表强迫，会让程序变成 逼迫用户 的工具，宣传文案绝不会这样说，色彩冲突。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"order"},{"key":"B","text":"track"},{"key":"C","text":"pace"},{"key":"D","text":"hold"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"16.","reason":"of your progress 表示 跟踪进度 The program keeps __(16)__ of your progress and provides detailed feedback __(17)__ your performance and improvement：程序追踪进度、提供反馈，需要 跟踪/记录 含义的搭配，正合 keep track of（跟踪记录）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"order = keep order 表 维持秩序，宾语是场合，不接 of progress，搭配不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"track + of = keep track of（跟踪记录），与 your progress 搭配地道，与下文 provides detailed feedback 顺承。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"pace = keep pace with（与……保持同步），但本句是 of 不是 with，搭配错。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"hold = keep hold of 表 紧握住，对象通常是物体或抽象的控制权，与 progress（进度）搭配不自然。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"on"},{"key":"B","text":"to"},{"key":"C","text":"for"},{"key":"D","text":"with"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"17.","reason":"feedback on something 是高频地道用法 provides detailed feedback __(17)__ your performance and improvement 表 提供关于你表现和进步的反馈，固定搭配 feedback on something 表 关于某事的反馈，正合本句语义。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"on 与 feedback 搭成 feedback on（关于……的反馈），是英语中最常见、最地道的搭配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"to 与 feedback 搭配会表 反馈给某人，对象应是人；这里 your performance 是事项而非人，搭配不当。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"for 表用途/目的，feedback for 含 为……提供反馈 的强加目的色彩，本句要表的是 关于……的反馈，搭配方向不对。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"with 与 feedback 搭配少见，且带 伴随、附带 含义，不能引出反馈的内容/主题，不合搭配。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"habitually"},{"key":"B","text":"constantly"},{"key":"C","text":"irregularly"},{"key":"D","text":"unusually"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"18.","reason":"下句的 增加阻力、变换肌群 暗示动态调整 下文 much like a(n) __(20)__ exercise routine requires you to increase resistance and vary your muscle use：将程序与 训练计划 类比，强调 持续增加阻力、不断变化训练，对应程序应 不断地 调整游戏。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"habitually 表 出于习惯地，常修饰有意识行为的人，但 it 是程序、无意识可言，且程序的调整不是 习惯 而是 算法驱动，色彩不合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"constantly 表 持续不断地，对应程序持续追踪进度、不停调整游戏的特性，与下文 增加阻力、变换肌群 的训练动态完全契合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"irregularly 表 无规律地，与上文 systematically improve 的系统训练定位冲突。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"unusually 表 异常地/特别地，描述的是反常状态，但程序的调整是常规算法行为，没有 反常 含义。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"carry"},{"key":"B","text":"put"},{"key":"C","text":"build"},{"key":"D","text":"take"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"19.","reason":"the strengths you are developing 暗示扩大优势 to __(19)__ on the strengths you are developing 中 the strengths you are developing 是 正在培养的强项，下文又拿 增加阻力 类比，可见是 在已有优势上继续加固，正合 build on（在……基础上发展）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"carry + on = carry on（继续），后面常接 something 或 doing，但 carry on the strengths 不是英语习惯说法，搭配不合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"put + on = put on（穿戴、上演），与 strengths 搭配语义跑偏，不表 强化优势。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"build + on = build on（以……为基础发展、加固），与 the strengths you are developing 搭配地道，对应 在你正培养的优势上继续扩大，与全段 系统训练、动态调整 同向。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"take + on = take on（承担、呈现），与 strengths 搭配既无 强化 含义，又是名词错位，意思跑偏。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"idle"},{"key":"B","text":"risky"},{"key":"C","text":"familiar"},{"key":"D","text":"effective"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"20.","reason":"本体是有效的脑训练程序 it __(18)__ modifies and enhances the games you play to __(19)__ on the strengths you are developing 把程序刻画为 持续动态调整、培养优势 的 有效训练；类比对象训练计划也须是 effective（有效的），才能与本体匹配。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"idle 表 闲置的/懒散的，与 increase resistance 与 vary your muscle use 的积极训练形象完全相反。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"risky 带 高风险 含义，作者要为程序背书，不会引用一个 高风险的训练计划 作为正面类比对象。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"familiar 表 熟悉的，强调主体已知，但类比的重心是 训练计划要不断升级，与 familiar 静态色彩不合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"effective 表 有效的，正合 不断增加阻力、改变肌肉运动 的高质量训练形象，并与本体 brain training program 的有效性形成正向类比闭环。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"In order to \"change lives for the better\" and reduce \"dependency\", George Osborne, Chancellor of the Exchequer, introduced the \"upfront work search\" scheme. Only if the jobless arrive at the jobcentre with a CV, register for online job search, and start looking for work will they be eligible for benefit – and then they should report weekly rather than fortnightly. What could be more reasonable?"},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"More apparent reasonableness followed. There will now be a seven-day wait for the jobseeker's allowance. \"Those first few days should be spent looking for work, not looking to sign on,\" he claimed. \"We're doing these things because we know they help people stay off benefits and help those on benefits get into work faster.\" Help? Really? On first hearing, this was the socially concerned chancellor, trying to change lives for the better, complete with \"reforms\" to an obviously indulgent system that demands too little effort from the newly unemployed to find work, and subsidises laziness. What motivated him, we were to understand, was his zeal for \"fundamental fairness\" – protecting the taxpayer, controlling spending and ensuring that only the most deserving claimants received their benefits."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"Losing a job is hurting: you don't skip down to the jobcentre with a song in your heart, delighted at the prospect of doubling your income from the generous state. It is financially terrifying, psychologically embarrassing and you know that support is minimal and extraordinarily hard to get. You are now not wanted; you are now excluded from the work environment that offers purpose and structure in your life. Worse, the crucial income to feed yourself and your family and pay the bills has disappeared. Ask anyone newly unemployed what they want and the answer is always: a job."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"But in Osborneland, your first instinct is to fall into dependency – permanent dependency if you can get it – supported by a state only too ready to indulge your falsehood. It is as though 20 years of ever-tougher reforms of the job search and benefit administration system never happened. The principle of British welfare is no longer that you can insure yourself against the risk of unemployment and receive unconditional payments if the disaster happens. Even the very phrase \"jobseeker's allowance\" is about redefining the unemployed as a \"jobseeker\" who had no fundamental right to a benefit he or she has earned through making national insurance contributions. Instead, the claimant receives a time-limited \"allowance,\" conditional on actively seeking a job; no entitlement and no insurance, at £71.70 a week, one of the least generous in the EU."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"George Osborne's scheme was intended to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"encourage jobseekers' active engagement in job seeking."},{"key":"B","text":"provide the unemployed with easier access to benefits."},{"key":"C","text":"guarantee jobseekers' legitimate right to benefits."},{"key":"D","text":"motivate the unemployed to report voluntarily."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"George Osborne的计划旨在____","choicesZh":{"A":"鼓励求职者积极参与求职。","B":"为失业者提供更便捷的福利获取途径。","C":"保障求职者获得福利的合法权利。","D":"激励失业者主动报告。"},"analysis":{"type":"George Osborne's scheme was intended to____ 直接询问方案的具体设立目的，回到原文 Osborne 介绍方案的那两句即可对应，没有 infer/imply 这类推断信号。","parse":"George Osborne's scheme was intended to____ 是 was intended to do 的被动结构，主语是 scheme，to 后接选项里的动词原形短语，等同于 the scheme was designed to do sth.，结构平铺直叙、无陷阱。","locateEn":"In order to \"change lives for the better\" and reduce \"dependency\", George Osborne, Chancellor of the Exchequer, introduced the \"upfront work search\" scheme. Only if the jobless arrive at the jobcentre with a CV, register for online job search, and start looking for work will they be eligible for benefit – and then they should report weekly rather than fortnightly.","locateZh":"为了\"改善人们的生活\"并减少\"依赖\"，财政大臣 George Osborne 推出了\"提前求职\"方案。失业者只有带着简历到就业中心、登记网上求职并开始找工作，才有资格领取救济，而且要每周（而非每两周）报到一次。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判说的\"逼失业者主动求职才发钱\"与 encourage jobseekers' active engagement in job seeking 在语义上一致，A 直接对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"Only if the jobless arrive at the jobcentre with a CV, register for online job search, and start looking for work will they be eligible for benefit","opt":"encourage jobseekers' active engagement in job seeking"},{"orig":"will they be eligible for benefit","opt":"encourage"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文方案在领钱前加了简历、登记、找工作、每周报到等门槛，是 easier 的反面，provide the unemployed with easier access to benefits 与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文方案是给领钱设条件，全文乃至第 4 段反而批评这种设计削弱了原本的权利；guarantee jobseekers' legitimate right to benefits 在原文里找不到对应表述。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"motivate the unemployed to report voluntarily 中 voluntarily 与原文 they should report weekly rather than fortnightly 的强制性 should 相反，方案是逼着报到，不是鼓励自愿。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"The phrase \"to sign on\" (Line 3, Para. 2) most probably means____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to check on the availability of jobs at the jobcentre."},{"key":"B","text":"to accept the government's restrictions on the allowance."},{"key":"C","text":"to register for an allowance from the government."},{"key":"D","text":"to attend a governmental job-training program."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"短语\"to sign on\"(第2段第3行)最可能的意思是____","choicesZh":{"A":"到就业中心查询职位空缺情况。","B":"接受政府对救济金的限制条件。","C":"向政府登记申请救济金。","D":"参加政府的职业培训项目。"},"analysis":{"type":"The phrase \"to sign on\" (Line 3, Para. 2) most probably means____ 直接询问一个加引号短语在原文中的意思，是典型的词义/短语题。","parse":"The phrase \"to sign on\" (Line 3, Para. 2) most probably means____ 主干是 The phrase means…，most probably 是程度副词，承认答案是上下文里最贴近的一项，并非唯一确解，提示要做语义比对，不是机械翻译。","locateEn":"\"Those first few days should be spent looking for work, not looking to sign on,\" he claimed.","locateZh":"他声称：\"那最初几天应当用来找工作，而不是用来登记领救济。\"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"to check on the availability of jobs at the jobcentre 描述的是查岗位信息，与原文把 sign on 放在 looking for work 的对立面相矛盾——如果 sign on 也是找工作，作者就不会把它和 looking for work 对立。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"to accept the government's restrictions on the allowance 谈的是接受限制，原文 sign on 是去办登记领救济的动作，文章并未把 sign on 与\"接受限制\"挂钩。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判说的\"去申领救济金\"与 to register for an allowance from the government 几乎逐字对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"looking to sign on","opt":"to register for an allowance from the government"},{"orig":"There will now be a seven-day wait for the jobseeker's allowance","opt":"an allowance from the government"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"to attend a governmental job-training program 谈的是参加培训项目，原文 sign on 仅指登记申领救济，整篇文章未提及任何 job-training program。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"What prompted the chancellor to develop his scheme?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A desire to secure a better life for all."},{"key":"B","text":"An eagerness to protect the unemployed."},{"key":"C","text":"An urge to be generous to the claimants."},{"key":"D","text":"A passion to ensure fairness for taxpayers."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"是什么促使财政大臣制定他的计划?","choicesZh":{"A":"希望为所有人保障更好的生活。","B":"渴望保护失业者。","C":"希望对申领者慷慨大方。","D":"热衷于确保纳税人的公平。"},"analysis":{"type":"What prompted the chancellor to develop his scheme? 直接问是什么促成 chancellor 推方案，对应原文中说明动机的那一句，无推断信号词。","parse":"What prompted the chancellor to develop his scheme? 主干是 What prompted sb. to do sth.，prompt 在这里是及物动词，主语 What 问的是动因，to develop his scheme 是结果状语，结构简单、无陷阱。","locateEn":"What motivated him, we were to understand, was his zeal for \"fundamental fairness\" – protecting the taxpayer, controlling spending and ensuring that only the most deserving claimants received their benefits.","locateZh":"我们被告知，促动他的是他对\"根本公平\"的热忱——也就是保护纳税人、控制开支、确保只有最该领救济的人才能领到救济。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A desire to secure a better life for all 中的 for all 把受益对象扩大到全体国民，与原文 only the most deserving claimants received their benefits 严格限定的\"最该领的人\"相冲突；首段 change lives for the better 是方案的宣传口号，而问题问的是真正动机。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"An eagerness to protect the unemployed 把保护对象写成失业者，但原文动机句中 protecting 的宾语是 the taxpayer，不是 the unemployed；作者第 3、4 段还专门论证方案恰恰伤害了失业者。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"An urge to be generous to the claimants 与原文 controlling spending 直接相反——控制开支恰恰是收紧而不是慷慨。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判中的\"对公平的热情\"+\"保护纳税人\"两项核心信息正好对应 A passion to ensure fairness for taxpayers 的三个核心词 passion、fairness、taxpayers。","pairs":[{"orig":"his zeal for \"fundamental fairness\"","opt":"A passion to ensure fairness"},{"orig":"protecting the taxpayer","opt":"for taxpayers"}]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"According to Paragraph 3, being unemployed makes one feel____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"uneasy."},{"key":"B","text":"insulted."},{"key":"C","text":"enraged."},{"key":"D","text":"guilty."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第3段,失业会让人感到____","choicesZh":{"A":"不安。","B":"受辱。","C":"愤怒。","D":"内疚。"},"analysis":{"type":"According to Paragraph 3, being unemployed makes one feel____ 限定段落、问具体感受，属于段内信息归纳，本质仍是细节题。","parse":"being unemployed makes one feel____ 是动名词短语 being unemployed 作主语 + makes one feel + 形容词的使役结构，空格处必须是描述感受的形容词，提醒考生选项应是单个情绪形容词，而非动作。","locateEn":"Losing a job is hurting: you don't skip down to the jobcentre with a song in your heart, delighted at the prospect of doubling your income from the generous state. It is financially terrifying, psychologically embarrassing and you know that support is minimal and extraordinarily hard to get.","locateZh":"失业是痛苦的：你不会哼着小调蹦蹦跳跳地去就业中心，对从慷慨的国家手里翻倍领钱感到兴奋。失业在经济上让人胆寒、在心理上让人难堪，而且你知道援助少得可怜、又极难拿到。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判出的\"焦虑不安、心里没着落\"与 uneasy 在极性（负面）与强度（中等、非极端）上完全一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"hurting","opt":"uneasy"},{"orig":"financially terrifying, psychologically embarrassing","opt":"uneasy"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"insulted 强调被他人侮辱、人格被攻击，原文 psychologically embarrassing 只是心理上难堪、尴尬，主体是失业者自身感受、并无他人施加侮辱的动作。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"enraged 指被激怒、暴怒，原文整段写的是失业者的恐惧、尴尬、无助，第 3 段没有任何愤怒/抗议的字眼。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"guilty 表示自责/有罪感，原文写失业者 You are now not wanted; you are now excluded from the work environment，描绘的是被排斥的无助感，而非道德上的愧疚。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"To which of the following would the author most probably agree?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Unemployment benefits should not be made conditional."},{"key":"B","text":"The British welfare system indulges jobseekers' laziness."},{"key":"C","text":"The jobseekers' allowance has met their actual needs."},{"key":"D","text":"Osborne's reforms will reduce the risk of unemployment."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者最可能同意以下哪一项?","choicesZh":{"A":"失业救济金不应附加条件。","B":"英国福利制度纵容求职者的懒惰。","C":"求职者津贴已经满足了他们的实际需求。","D":"Osborne的改革将降低失业风险。"},"analysis":{"type":"To which of the following would the author most probably agree? 没有给关键词，是问作者会同意四个观点中的哪一个，需要把全文的立场综合后再下判。","parse":"To which of the following would the author most probably agree? 是 agree to which 的倒装疑问句，正常语序是 the author would most probably agree to which of the following，提醒考生四个选项是 agree 的宾语，需作者赞同的才是答案。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判出的\"反对救济金附条件化\"与 Unemployment benefits should not be made conditional 在主张方向上一致，A 是作者会赞同的命题。","pairs":[{"orig":"Even the very phrase \"jobseeker's allowance\" is about redefining the unemployed as a \"jobseeker\" who had no fundamental right to a benefit he or she has earned through making national insurance contributions","opt":"Unemployment benefits should not be made conditional"},{"orig":"Instead, the claimant receives a time-limited \"allowance,\" conditional on actively seeking a job; no entitlement and no insurance","opt":"Unemployment benefits should not be made conditional"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"The British welfare system indulges jobseekers' laziness 是 Osborne 在第 2 段背后的指控（subsidises laziness），作者用反问和情绪铺陈反驳了它，不会赞同该观点。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"The jobseekers' allowance has met their actual needs 与原文 support is minimal and extraordinarily hard to get 及 £71.70 a week, one of the least generous in the EU 严重相反，作者不会赞同。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Osborne's reforms will reduce the risk of unemployment 把方案效果说成降低\"失业风险\"，原文方案针对的只是领救济流程、并未承诺也未被作者承认能减少失业本身，作者本就质疑方案对失业者有任何 Help。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"All around the world, lawyers generate more hostility than the members of any other profession – with the possible exception of journalism. But there are few places where clients have more grounds for complaint than America."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"During the decade before the economic crisis, spending on legal services in America grew twice as fast as inflation. The best lawyers made skyscrapers-full of money, tempting ever more students to pile into law schools. But most law graduates never get a big-firm job. Many of them instead become the kind of nuisance-lawsuit filer that makes the tort system a costly nightmare."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"There are many reasons for this. One is the excessive costs of a legal education. There is just one path for a lawyer in most American states: a four-year undergraduate degree in some unrelated subject, then a three-year law degree at one of 200 law schools authorized by the American Bar Association and an expensive preparation for the bar exam. This leaves today's average law-school graduate with $100,000 of debt on top of undergraduate debts. Law-school debt means that they have to work fearsomely hard."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"Reforming the system would help both lawyers and their customers. Sensible ideas have been around for a long time, but the state-level bodies that govern the profession have been too conservative to implement them. One idea is to allow people to study law as an undergraduate degree. Another is to let students sit for the bar after only two years of law school. If the bar exam is truly a stern enough test for a would-be lawyer, those who can sit it earlier should be allowed to do so. Students who do not need the extra training could cut their debt mountain by a third."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"The other reason why costs are so high is the restrictive guild-like ownership structure of the business. Except in the District of Columbia, non-lawyers may not own any share of a law firm. This keeps fees high and innovation slow. There is pressure for change from within the profession, but opponents of change among the regulators insist that keeping outsiders out of a law firm isolates lawyers from the pressure to make money rather than serve clients ethically."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-6","text":"In fact, allowing non-lawyers to own shares in law firms would reduce costs and improve services to customers, by encouraging law firms to use technology and to employ professional managers to focus on improving firms' efficiency. After all, other countries, such as Australia and Britain, have started liberalizing their legal professions. America should follow."}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"A lot of students take up law as their profession due to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the growing demand from clients."},{"key":"B","text":"the increasing pressure of inflation."},{"key":"C","text":"the prospect of working in big firms."},{"key":"D","text":"the attraction of financial rewards."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"许多学生选择法律作为职业是由于____","choicesZh":{"A":"客户需求的不断增长。","B":"通货膨胀压力的不断增加。","C":"在大型律所工作的前景。","D":"经济回报的吸引力。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 A lot of students take up law as their profession due to 是一句具体事实+原因填空，落点在某段定位句，不是全局推断或主旨。","parse":"A lot of students take up law as their profession due to____：主干是 students take up law，as their profession 是 take up 的方式状语，due to 引出原因短语作状语，整句平铺直叙、无陷阱。","locateEn":"The best lawyers made skyscrapers-full of money, tempting ever more students to pile into law schools.","locateZh":"顶尖律师赚得堆积如山的财富，吸引越来越多的学生扎堆涌入法学院。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"the growing demand from clients 文中只字未提客户需求增加，原文相邻处只有 spending on legal services in America grew twice as fast as inflation，谈的是花费增长而非需求增长，且也未把它与学生选法学挂钩。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 spending on legal services in America grew twice as fast as inflation 中 inflation 只是\"做对比的参照系\"，并非吸引学生学法律的原因；the increasing pressure of inflation 把参照对象偷换成驱动力。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 most law graduates never get a big-firm job 明说多数毕业生根本进不了大所，the prospect of working in big firms 把\"少数人的实际去向\"误读成\"普遍吸引诱因\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判的\"赚很多钱吸引人\"在四项中只有 the attraction of financial rewards 与之一一对应，其它三项均与定位句无对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"The best lawyers made skyscrapers-full of money, tempting ever more students to pile into law schools","opt":"the attraction of financial rewards"}]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"Which of the following adds to the costs of legal education in most American states?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Higher tuition fees for undergraduate studies."},{"key":"B","text":"Receiving training by professional associations."},{"key":"C","text":"Admissions approval from the bar association."},{"key":"D","text":"Pursuing a bachelor's degree in another major."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"以下哪一项增加了美国大多数州的法律教育成本?","choicesZh":{"A":"本科学习的学费更高。","B":"接受专业协会的培训。","C":"律师协会的入会批准。","D":"攻读另一专业的学士学位。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following adds to the costs 是从四项里挑出推高成本的那一项，本质是要在原文找出某条具体做法并和选项对应。","parse":"Which of the following adds to the costs of legal education in most American states?：主语是 Which of the following，谓语 adds to（加剧/推高），介词短语 in most American states 限定范围。注意 add to 不是 add up，意为\"增添\"，非\"加起来\"。","locateEn":"There is just one path for a lawyer in most American states: a four-year undergraduate degree in some unrelated subject, then a three-year law degree at one of 200 law schools authorized by the American Bar Association and an expensive preparation for the bar exam.","locateZh":"在美国多数州，想成为律师只有一条路：先在某个无关学科念四年本科，再到 200 所获美国律师协会认证的法学院之一读三年法律学位，外加一段花费不菲的律师资格考试备考。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Higher tuition fees for undergraduate studies 谈\"本科学费高\"，但原文只说要读一个\"无关本科\"作为先决条件，从未比较其学费高低，更未将其作为致贵环节。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 an expensive preparation for the bar exam 是\"为律师资格考试做备考\"，Receiving training by professional associations 偷换成\"接受专业协会的培训\"，主语与施动者都不同。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 200 law schools authorized by the American Bar Association 明说律师协会认证的是\"法学院\"，Admissions approval from the bar association 误读成\"考生须经律师协会批准入学\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"在定位句列出的三段花费里，只有\"先读一个无关本科\"被选项 Pursuing a bachelor's degree in another major 精确对应，且它正是文章后文要建议改革的环节，强化为本题答案。","pairs":[{"orig":"a four-year undergraduate degree in some unrelated subject","opt":"Pursuing a bachelor's degree in another major"}]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"Hindrance to the reform of the legal system originates from____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the rigid bodies governing the profession."},{"key":"B","text":"lawyers' and clients' strong resistance."},{"key":"C","text":"the stern exam for would-be lawyers."},{"key":"D","text":"non-professionals' sharp criticism."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"法律制度改革的障碍源于____","choicesZh":{"A":"管理该行业的僵化机构。","B":"律师和客户的强烈抵制。","C":"准律师的严格考试。","D":"非专业人士的尖锐批评。"},"analysis":{"type":"Hindrance…originates from 要的是文章明写的归因，不是要你推断，对应的应是原文一句直接陈述。","parse":"Hindrance to the reform of the legal system originates from____：主语 Hindrance to the reform of the legal system（of+of 双层修饰：对法律体制之改革之阻碍），谓语 originates from，空格填名词性短语作宾语。两层 of 嵌套可能让基础薄弱的考生绕晕，把它读成\"阻碍\"+\"改革\"+\"法律体制\"三层即可。","locateEn":"Sensible ideas have been around for a long time, but the state-level bodies that govern the profession have been too conservative to implement them.","locateZh":"明智的改革方案早已存在多年，但管理该行业的州一级机构一直过于保守，无法将其付诸实施。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判的\"州级管理机构太保守\"与 the rigid bodies governing the profession 精确对位，rigid 是 too conservative 的标准同义概括，锁定 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"the state-level bodies that govern the profession","opt":"the rigid bodies governing the profession"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Reforming the system would help both lawyers and their customers 明说律师和客户都会从改革中受益，根本不是阻力；lawyers' and clients' strong resistance 与原文立场相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 If the bar exam is truly a stern enough test for a would-be lawyer, those who can sit it earlier should be allowed to do so 中\"stern test\"是改革派用来支持\"提前考\"的假设前提，并非阻挡改革的因素，the stern exam for would-be lawyers 张冠李戴。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"本段及全文均未提及\"非专业人士对法律体系的尖锐批评\"，non-professionals' sharp criticism 系凭空捏造。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"The guild-like ownership structure is considered \"restrictive\" partly because it____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"prevents lawyers from gaining due profits."},{"key":"B","text":"bans outsiders' involvement in the profession."},{"key":"C","text":"aggravates the ethical situation in the trade."},{"key":"D","text":"keeps lawyers from holding law-firm shares."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"行会式所有权结构被认为具有\"限制性\",部分原因是它____","choicesZh":{"A":"阻止律师获得应得的利润。","B":"禁止外部人员参与该行业。","C":"加剧了该行业的道德状况。","D":"阻止律师持有律所股份。"},"analysis":{"type":"partly because it____ 让你从原文里找到\"为什么这个结构是限制性的\"的某一条理由，定位精确、对应明确，是细节题。","parse":"The guild-like ownership structure is considered \"restrictive\" partly because it____：主干是 The structure is considered restrictive，partly because it____ 是原因状语从句，it 指代 The guild-like ownership structure。空格在 it 之后，要填动词性短语，做从句的谓语+宾语。","locateEn":"Except in the District of Columbia, non-lawyers may not own any share of a law firm.","locateZh":"除华盛顿特区外，非律师不得持有律所的任何股份。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说 This keeps fees high，即拉高客户付费，并未说律师拿不到应得利润；prevents lawyers from gaining due profits 把方向写反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"禁外行进入持股\"与 bans outsiders' involvement in the profession 精确对应，且与同段后文 keeping outsiders out of a law firm 反向印证，锁定 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"non-lawyers may not own any share of a law firm","opt":"bans outsiders' involvement in the profession"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 opponents of change among the regulators insist that keeping outsiders out of a law firm isolates lawyers from the pressure to make money rather than serve clients ethically 表述的是反对改革者的观点：现状反而保护职业操守；选项 aggravates the ethical situation in the trade 说\"恶化\"，与该陈述方向相反，且把对方观点当成作者结论。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 non-lawyers may not own any share of a law firm 说的是非律师不得持股，keeps lawyers from holding law-firm shares 把禁令对象从\"非律师\"偷换成\"律师\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"In this text, the author mainly discusses____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the factors that help make a successful lawyer in America."},{"key":"B","text":"a problem in America's legal profession and solutions to it."},{"key":"C","text":"the role of undergraduate studies in America's legal education."},{"key":"D","text":"flawed ownership of America's law firms and its causes."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"在本文中,作者主要讨论____","choicesZh":{"A":"帮助在美国成为成功律师的因素。","B":"美国法律行业的一个问题及其解决方案。","C":"本科学习在美国法律教育中的作用。","D":"美国律所所有权的缺陷及其原因。"},"analysis":{"type":"In this text, the author mainly discusses____ 直接问全文主旨，是典型主旨题题干。","parse":"In this text, the author mainly discusses____：状语 In this text + 主语 the author + 谓语 mainly discusses + 空格作宾语，结构极简，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"the factors that help make a successful lawyer in America 把话题改成\"如何成为成功律师\"，原文除 The best lawyers made skyscrapers-full of money 一笔带过外，完全没讨论成功律师的成因。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"四项中只有 a problem in America's legal profession and solutions to it 同时覆盖\"问题+解决方案\"双线，且\"a problem\"用单数也契合作者把多条成因统归一题的论述口径。","pairs":[{"orig":"One is the excessive costs of a legal education","opt":"a problem in America's legal profession and solutions to it"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"本科非法专业只是 P3 提到的局部成因之一，并由 One idea is to allow people to study law as an undergraduate degree 当作可改革点；the role of undergraduate studies in America's legal education 把局部成因当作全文主旨，明显以偏概全。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"flawed ownership of America's law firms and its causes 只覆盖 P5 一段的股权话题，丢掉了 P3 法学教育成本与 P4、P6 的方案与呼吁；另外作者重点是\"开放后的好处与建议\"，而不是\"股权缺陷的成因\"。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"The US $3-million Fundamental Physics Prize is indeed an interesting experiment, as Alexander Polyakov said when he accepted this year's award in March. And it is far from the only one of its type. As a News Feature article in Nature discusses, a string of lucrative awards for researchers have joined the Nobel Prizes in recent years. Many, like the Fundamental Physics Prize, are funded from the telephone-number-sized bank accounts of Internet entrepreneurs. These benefactors have succeeded in their chosen fields, they say, and they want to use their wealth to draw attention to those who have succeeded in science."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"What's not to like? Quite a lot, according to a handful of scientists quoted in the News Feature. You cannot buy class, as the old saying goes, and these upstart entrepreneurs cannot buy their prizes the prestige of the Nobels. The new awards are an exercise in self-promotion for those behind them, say scientists. They could distort the achievement-based system of peer-review-led research. They could cement the status quo of peer-reviewed research. They do not fund peer-reviewed research. They perpetuate the myth of the lone genius."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"The goals of the prize-givers seem as scattered as the criticism. Some want to shock, others to draw people into science, or to better reward those who have made their careers in research."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"As Nature has pointed out before, there are some legitimate concerns about how science prizes – both new and old – are distributed. The Breakthrough Prize in Life Sciences, launched this year, takes an unrepresentative view of what the life sciences include. But the Nobel Foundation's limit of three recipients per prize, each of whom must still be living, has long been outgrown by the collaborative nature of modern research – as will be demonstrated by the inevitable row over who is ignored when it comes to acknowledging the discovery of the Higgs boson. The Nobels were, of course, themselves set up by a very rich individual who had decided what he wanted to do with his own money. Time, rather than intention, has given them legitimacy."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"As much as some scientists may complain about the new awards, two things seem clear. First, most researchers would accept such a prize if they were offered one. Second, it is surely a good thing that the money and attention come to science rather than go elsewhere. It is fair to criticize and question the mechanism – that is the culture of research, after all – but it is the prize-givers' money to do with as they please. It is wise to take such gifts with gratitude and grace."}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"The Fundamental Physics Prize is seen as____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a symbol of the entrepreneurs' wealth."},{"key":"B","text":"a handsome reward for researchers."},{"key":"C","text":"a possible replacement of the Nobel Prizes."},{"key":"D","text":"an example of bankers' investments."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"基础物理学奖被视为____","choicesZh":{"A":"企业家财富的象征。","B":"对研究人员的丰厚奖励。","C":"诺贝尔奖的可能替代者。","D":"银行家投资的一个例子。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The Fundamental Physics Prize is seen as____ 问的是该奖项 \"被视为什么\"，是对一个具体对象的客观定性，没有 infer/imply 等推断信号词。","parse":"The Fundamental Physics Prize is seen as____ 是 \"主语 + 系动词 + 介词短语\" 的不完整陈述句，被动语态 is seen as 等同于 \"is regarded as\"，下划线处由选项补足表语；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"The US $3-million Fundamental Physics Prize is indeed an interesting experiment, as Alexander Polyakov said when he accepted this year's award in March.","locateZh":"正如 Alexander Polyakov 三月份领奖时所说，这项 300 万美元的基础物理奖确实是一次有趣的尝试。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文说 they want to use their wealth to draw attention to those who have succeeded in science——出资者的目的是把注意力引向科学家，而不是用这笔钱来 \"象征自己的财富\"。选项 a symbol of the entrepreneurs' wealth 把 \"使用财富的工具\" 偷换成 \"财富的象征\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判的 \"奖金巨额的科研奖\" 与 a handsome reward for researchers 完全对应——handsome 接住巨额，researchers 接住科研获奖者，故选 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"The US $3-million Fundamental Physics Prize","opt":"a handsome reward"},{"orig":"those who have succeeded in science","opt":"for researchers"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 a string of lucrative awards for researchers have joined the Nobel Prizes 用 joined 表达 \"与诺奖并立\"，选项 a possible replacement of the Nobel Prizes 把 \"加入\" 升级为 \"取代\"，属过度推断。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 Internet entrepreneurs 指 \"互联网企业家\"，选项 an example of bankers' investments 偷换成 \"银行家\"；且 \"investments\" 把 \"捐赠 / 奖金\" 偷换为 \"投资\"，双重偷换。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"The critics think that the new awards will most benefit____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the profit-oriented scientists."},{"key":"B","text":"the achievement-based system."},{"key":"C","text":"the founders of the new awards."},{"key":"D","text":"peer-review-led research."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"批评者认为新奖项将最有利于____","choicesZh":{"A":"以营利为导向的科学家。","B":"基于成就的体系。","C":"新奖项的创立者。","D":"同行评审主导的研究。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The critics think that the new awards will most benefit____ 要求复述批评者的具体观点，属于立场观点的细节复现，而非延伸推断。","parse":"The critics think that the new awards will most benefit____ 主句是 The critics think，that 引导宾语从句，从句主语 the new awards、谓语 will most benefit 缺宾语，由选项补足；结构清晰，无陷阱。","locateEn":"The new awards are an exercise in self-promotion for those behind them, say scientists.","locateZh":"科学家们说，这些新奖项不过是奖项幕后之人的自我营销之举。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未出现 \"profit-oriented scientists（逐利科学家）\" 这一群体，更未说他们最受益，纯属虚构。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文说新奖项 could distort the achievement-based system of peer-review-led research——批评者认为新奖项会扭曲（损害）这一机制，选项却说它最受益，与原文极性相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判 \"幕后出资人最受益\" 直接锁 the founders of the new awards，那些幕后之人就是奖项创立者本人。","pairs":[{"orig":"those behind them","opt":"the founders of the new awards"},{"orig":"an exercise in self-promotion","opt":"the founders of the new awards"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 They do not fund peer-reviewed research 明确说新奖项不资助同行评审研究，对该研究并无 benefit；选项却称其最受益，正话反说。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"The discovery of the Higgs boson is a typical case which involves____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"legitimate concerns over the new prizes."},{"key":"B","text":"controversies over the recipients' status."},{"key":"C","text":"the joint effort of modern researchers."},{"key":"D","text":"the demonstration of research findings."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"希格斯玻色子的发现是一个典型案例,它涉及____","choicesZh":{"A":"对新奖项的合理担忧。","B":"关于获奖者资格的争议。","C":"现代研究人员的共同努力。","D":"研究成果的展示。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The discovery of the Higgs boson is a typical case which involves____ 不问例子细节，而问 \"这个例子卷入 / 涉及什么\"，本质是问例子用来证明哪个观点。","parse":"The discovery of the Higgs boson is a typical case which involves____ 主语为长名词短语 The discovery of the Higgs boson，which 引导限制性定语从句修饰 a typical case，which 在从句中作主语、involves 后缺宾语由选项补足。","locateEn":"But the Nobel Foundation's limit of three recipients per prize, each of whom must still be living, has long been outgrown by the collaborative nature of modern research – as will be demonstrated by the inevitable row over who is ignored when it comes to acknowledging the discovery of the Higgs boson.","locateZh":"然而，诺贝尔基金会 \"每个奖项最多三位获奖者且每位都必须健在\" 的规定，早已被现代科研的协作性质所撑破——这一点将在表彰希格斯玻色子发现时关于 \"谁被忽略\" 的不可避免的争论中得到证明。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"legitimate concerns over the new prizes 出自 there are some legitimate concerns about how science prizes – both new and old – are distributed——但 legitimate concerns 是用来形容整体的奖项分配问题，与希格斯玻色子的例证无直接关联；希格斯玻色子直接证明的是 \"诺奖规则被撑破\"，不是 \"新奖项的合理质疑\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文争论点是 who is ignored——谁被忽略，焦点在 \"漏掉的人\"；选项 controversies over the recipients' status 把焦点偷换成 \"获奖者的地位\"，地位与是否被忽略不是同一回事。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判 \"现代科研的协作本质\" 与 the joint effort of modern researchers 一一对应，故选 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"the collaborative nature of modern research","opt":"the joint effort of modern researchers"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"选项 the demonstration of research findings 利用了原文 as will be demonstrated by 中的 demonstrated 字面，但原文的 demonstrate 是 \"证明（某论点）\"，而非 \"展示（研究成果）\"；选项偷换为 \"研究成果的展示\"，与例证目的毫无关联。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"According to Paragraph 4, which of the following is true of the Nobels?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"History has never cast doubt on them."},{"key":"B","text":"Their endurance has done justice to them."},{"key":"C","text":"They are the most representative honor."},{"key":"D","text":"Their legitimacy has long been in dispute."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第4段,关于诺贝尔奖以下哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"历史从未对它们产生过质疑。","B":"它们的持久性证明了它们的公正性。","C":"它们是最具代表性的荣誉。","D":"它们的合法性长期以来一直存在争议。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 which of the following is true of the Nobels? 是典型的 \"以下哪项符合原文\" 选项级真伪判断，依据严格限定在 Paragraph 4 内。","parse":"According to Paragraph 4, which of the following is true of the Nobels? 主句为 which 引导的特殊疑问句，According to Paragraph 4 是状语限定信息来源，of the Nobels 修饰主语 which；结构简单，关键是看清范围限定在第四段。","locateEn":"The Nobels were, of course, themselves set up by a very rich individual who had decided what he wanted to do with his own money. Time, rather than intention, has given them legitimacy.","locateZh":"诺贝尔奖本身也是由一位大富翁设立的——他自己决定怎么用自己的钱。是时间、而不是初心，赋予了诺奖合法性。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 Time, rather than intention, has given them legitimacy 承认是时间最终赋予合法性，但这恰恰反向暗示历史上对其合法性曾有疑虑——否则不需要 \"时间来赋予\"；选项 History has never cast doubt on them 用 never 把可能存在的疑虑彻底否决，属过度推断到绝对极端。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判 \"时间赋予合法性\" 与 Their endurance has done justice to them 完全对应——endurance 接 Time、has done justice to them 接 has given them legitimacy，故选 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"Time","opt":"Their endurance"},{"orig":"has given them legitimacy","opt":"has done justice to them"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文在第四段反而指出现有奖项（包括诺奖）的代表性问题——Breakthrough Prize in Life Sciences ... takes an unrepresentative view 及诺奖三人上限不堪现代协作之重；选项 They are the most representative honor 称诺奖 \"最具代表性\"，与全段批评意旨相反，且 \"最 representative\" 一说原文从未出现。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 Time, rather than intention, has given them legitimacy 是 \"已经赋予了合法性\"——是已完成的结论；选项 Their legitimacy has long been in dispute 却称 \"合法性长期处于争议中\"，把已尘埃落定的现在完成事实偷换成持续的争议状态。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"The author believes that the new awards are____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"unworthy of public attention."},{"key":"B","text":"subject to undesirable changes."},{"key":"C","text":"harmful to the culture of research."},{"key":"D","text":"acceptable despite the criticism."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者认为新奖项____","choicesZh":{"A":"不值得公众关注。","B":"会受到不良变化的影响。","C":"有害于研究文化。","D":"尽管受到批评但仍可接受。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The author believes that the new awards are____ 显式询问作者本人的看法，是态度题的标准句式。","parse":"The author believes that the new awards are____ 主句 The author believes，that 引导宾语从句；从句主语 the new awards、系动词 are 后缺表语由选项补足；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 it is surely a good thing that the money and attention come to science 明确说 \"钱和关注流向科学是件好事\"，作者认为新奖项值得公众关注；选项 unworthy of public attention 说 \"不值得公众关注\"，与作者立场极性相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"subject to undesirable changes 称新奖项会经历 \"不良变化\"，但原文从未提及 \"会发生不良变化\" 这一论断——既无 \"changes\" 也无 \"undesirable\" 在 P5 中作用于新奖项。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 it is the prize-givers' money to do with as they please 与 It is wise to take such gifts with gratitude and grace 体现作者认为新奖项对科研文化无害、应当接纳；选项 harmful to the culture of research 说 \"有害于科研文化\"，与作者末段评价反向。注意 that is the culture of research, after all 中 \"批评和质疑机制本身才是科研文化\"——批评新奖是研究文化的体现，而不是新奖在伤害文化。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判 \"尽管存在批评，新奖项仍是可以接受的\" 与 acceptable despite the criticism 完全对应——despite the criticism 接 As much as some scientists may complain，acceptable 接 wise to take，故选 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"As much as some scientists may complain about the new awards","opt":"despite the criticism"},{"orig":"It is wise to take such gifts with gratitude and grace","opt":"acceptable"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"\"The Heart of the Matter,\" the just-released report by the American Academy of Arts and Sciences (AAAS), deserves praise for affirming the importance of the humanities and social sciences to the prosperity and security of liberal democracy in America. Regrettably, however, the report's failure to address the true nature of the crisis facing liberal education may cause more harm than good."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"In 2010, leading congressional Democrats and Republicans sent letters to the AAAS asking that it identify actions that could be taken by \"federal, state and local governments, universities, foundations, educators, individual benefactors and others\" to \"maintain national excellence in humanities and social scientific scholarship and education.\" In response, the American Academy formed the Commission on the Humanities and Social Sciences. Among the commission's 51 members are top-tier-university presidents, scholars, lawyers, judges, and business executives, as well as prominent figures from diplomacy, filmmaking, music and journalism."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"The goals identified in the report are generally admirable. Because representative government presupposes an informed citizenry, the report supports full literacy; stresses the study of history and government, particularly American history and American government; and encourages the use of new digital technologies. To encourage innovation and competition, the report calls for increased investment in research, the crafting of coherent curricula that improve students' ability to solve problems and communicate effectively in the 21st century, increased funding for teachers and the encouragement of scholars to bring their learning to bear on the great challenges of the day. The report also advocates greater study of foreign languages, international affairs and the expansion of study abroad programs."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"Unfortunately, despite 2½ years in the making, \"The Heart of the Matter\" never gets to the heart of the matter: the illiberal nature of liberal education at our leading colleges and universities. The commission ignores that for several decades America's colleges and universities have produced graduates who don't know the content and character of liberal education and are thus deprived of its benefits. Sadly, the spirit of inquiry once at home on campus has been replaced by the use of the humanities and social sciences as vehicles for publicizing \"progressive,\" or left-liberal propaganda."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"Today, professors routinely treat the progressive interpretation of history and progressive public policy as the proper subject of study while portraying conservative or classical liberal ideas – such as free markets and self-reliance – as falling outside the boundaries of routine, and sometimes legitimate, intellectual investigation."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"The AAAS displays great enthusiasm for liberal education. Yet its report may well set back reform by obscuring the depth and breadth of the challenge that Congress asked it to illuminate."}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"According to Paragraph 1, what is the author's attitude toward the AAAS's report?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Critical."},{"key":"B","text":"Appreciative."},{"key":"C","text":"Contemptuous."},{"key":"D","text":"Tolerant."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"态度题","stemZh":"根据第1段,作者对AAAS报告持什么态度?","choicesZh":{"A":"批评的。","B":"赞赏的。","C":"轻蔑的。","D":"宽容的。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 what is the author's attitude toward the AAAS's report 中出现 attitude，属于典型的态度判断题。","parse":"结构平直：主句 what is the author's attitude toward the AAAS's report，介词短语 toward... 限定态度的对象——AAAS 的那份报告。无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判段内真正立场在转折后的负面，Critical 是四个选项中唯一表达负面评价的词，自然锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"Regrettably, however, the report's failure to address the true nature of the crisis facing liberal education may cause more harm than good","opt":"Critical"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Appreciative 抓住了 deserves praise 这一让步面的肯定，但忽略了 however 之后的真正立场，是典型的只见让步不见转折。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Contemptuous 意为'轻蔑、鄙夷'，是强烈负面情绪；作者只是指出报告未切中要害，并无人格化的轻蔑情绪，强度严重失配。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Tolerant 意为'容忍、宽容'，含'纵使有缺点仍接受'的中性偏正面色彩，与作者明确批评报告未切要害的立场方向相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"Influential figures in the Congress required that the AAAS report on how to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"define the government's role in education."},{"key":"B","text":"safeguard individuals' rights to education."},{"key":"C","text":"retain people's interest in liberal education."},{"key":"D","text":"keep a leading position in liberal education."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"国会中有影响力的人物要求AAAS报告如何____","choicesZh":{"A":"界定政府在教育中的角色。","B":"保障个人受教育的权利。","C":"保持人们对人文教育的兴趣。","D":"保持在人文教育中的领先地位。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 report on how to 要求复述国会的具体诉求内容，是对原文事实的客观转述，不涉及推断。","parse":"题干是 required that ... 的不完整陈述句，空格处补完 how to 之后的不定式短语；要警惕国会诉求的内容是 'to + 动词' 的完整短语，不能只看到一两个关键词就下结论。","locateEn":"In 2010, leading congressional Democrats and Republicans sent letters to the AAAS asking that it identify actions that could be taken by \"federal, state and local governments, universities, foundations, educators, individual benefactors and others\" to \"maintain national excellence in humanities and social scientific scholarship and education.\"","locateZh":"2010 年，国会两党的主要议员致函 AAAS，请它确定可由 '联邦、州和地方政府、大学、基金会、教育者、个人资助者及其他主体' 采取的行动，以 '维持美国在人文与社会科学学术研究和教育上的全国卓越地位'。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"define the government's role in education 只截取了 federal, state and local governments 这一行动主体之一，把国会的整体诉求窄化为 '界定政府的角色'，但原文中 governments 只是众多主体清单的一员。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"safeguard individuals' rights to education 涉及的 'individuals' rights' 在原文中找不到对应概念，国会请求里既无 rights 也无 safeguard，是凭空添加的法律权利话题。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"retain people's interest in liberal education 把 maintain excellence （维持卓越地位）偷换成 retain interest （留住兴趣），后者关注公众兴趣度，前者关注学术领先地位，二者并非同义。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判要 '保住人文社科教育的领先地位'，keep a leading position in liberal education 在动词、形容词、宾语三个层面都与原文同义对应，是唯一完整对位的选项。","pairs":[{"orig":"maintain national excellence in humanities and social scientific scholarship and education","opt":"keep a leading position in liberal education"}]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"According to Paragraph 3, the report suggests____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"an exclusive study of American history."},{"key":"B","text":"a greater emphasis on theoretical subjects."},{"key":"C","text":"the application of emerging technologies."},{"key":"D","text":"funding for the study of foreign languages."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第3段,该报告建议____","choicesZh":{"A":"专门研究美国历史。","B":"更加重视理论学科。","C":"应用新兴技术。","D":"资助外语研究。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干要求复述报告中提出的具体建议，属事实归纳类细节题。","parse":"report suggests + 不完整宾语，空格处由选项补出宾语；注意选项中 only/exclusive/greater 这类范围/程度词，对应原文的 also/particularly 时常被偷换。","locateEn":"To encourage innovation and competition, the report calls for increased investment in research, the crafting of coherent curricula that improve students' ability to solve problems and communicate effectively in the 21st century, increased funding for teachers and the encouragement of scholars to bring their learning to bear on the great challenges of the day.","locateZh":"为鼓励创新与竞争，该报告呼吁增加对研究的投资，编制能提升学生在 21 世纪解决问题和有效沟通能力的连贯课程，加大对教师的资金支持，并鼓励学者运用其学识应对当今的重大挑战。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"an exclusive study of American history 的 exclusive（独占的、唯一的）将原文 particularly American history and American government 的 particularly（尤其、特别强调）做了范围放大——原文只说 '特别强调' 美国史，并未说 '只学' 美国史。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"a greater emphasis on theoretical subjects 强调 '理论性学科'，与原文重点不符——原文呼吁的是培养 students' ability to solve problems and communicate effectively 这类实践能力，是 problem-solving 而非 theoretical。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"清单 8 项中只有 '新数字技术' 这一条能找到选项一对一的对位，其他选项要么以偏概全要么无中生有。","pairs":[{"orig":"encourages the use of new digital technologies","opt":"the application of emerging technologies"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"funding for the study of foreign languages 把 increased funding for teachers 中的 funding 与 advocates greater study of foreign languages 中的 foreign languages 强行拼接，但原文中 funding 的对象是 teachers，study 的对象才是 foreign languages，二者并非同一句。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"The author implies in Paragraph 5 that professors are____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"supportive of free markets."},{"key":"B","text":"conservative about public policy."},{"key":"C","text":"biased against classical liberal ideas."},{"key":"D","text":"cautious about intellectual investigation."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"推断题","stemZh":"作者在第5段暗示教授们____","choicesZh":{"A":"支持自由市场。","B":"在公共政策方面保守。","C":"对古典自由主义理念有偏见。","D":"对学术探究持谨慎态度。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The author implies 用 imply 表明本题需要在段内事实上做一步推断。","parse":"句子简短：作者 implies that professors are + 形容词性表语；只需判断教授对哪类思想呈何种态度，关注段内 progressive 与 conservative 的对照即可。","locateEn":"Today, professors routinely treat the progressive interpretation of history and progressive public policy as the proper subject of study while portraying conservative or classical liberal ideas – such as free markets and self-reliance – as falling outside the boundaries of routine, and sometimes legitimate, intellectual investigation.","locateZh":"如今，教授们惯常地把进步派的历史解读与进步派公共政策视为正当的研究对象，与此同时却把保守派或古典自由派的观念——如自由市场和自立——描绘成超出常规、有时是超出正当智识探究范围的内容。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"supportive of free markets 称教授支持自由市场，但原文恰恰把 free markets and self-reliance 列为教授排斥的古典自由派观念——立场被反过来了。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"conservative about public policy 称教授对公共政策持保守立场，但原文明确教授把 progressive public policy（进步派公共政策）视为正当研究对象，立场是进步派而非保守派。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判教授对古典自由派观念抱有偏见，biased against classical liberal ideas 用 biased against 精准捕捉了 portray...as falling outside the boundaries 的偏待性，是唯一对位项。","pairs":[{"orig":"portraying conservative or classical liberal ideas – such as free markets and self-reliance – as falling outside the boundaries of routine, and sometimes legitimate, intellectual investigation","opt":"biased against classical liberal ideas"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"cautious about intellectual investigation 称教授对智识探究本身谨慎；原文是教授对一类思想（古典自由派）持排斥态度，并非对智识探究本身谨慎——把对象错位到 intellectual investigation 这个上位概念上。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Ways to Grasp \"The Heart of the Matter\""},{"key":"B","text":"Illiberal Education and \"The Heart of the Matter\""},{"key":"C","text":"The AAAS's Contribution to Liberal Education"},{"key":"D","text":"Progressive Policy vs. Liberal Education"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"以下哪项最适合作为本文标题?","choicesZh":{"A":"把握\"问题核心\"的方法","B":"非人文教育与\"问题核心\"","C":"AAAS对人文教育的贡献","D":"进步政策与人文教育"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 the best title for the text 直接问最佳标题，是主旨题的标准问法。","parse":"Which of the following 引导的特殊疑问句，问选项中哪一个最合适做标题，无理解陷阱；难度全部在与正文主旨的匹配。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Ways to Grasp \"The Heart of the Matter\" 暗示文章在教读者 '如何把握那份报告' 的方法，而本文是评论与批评，不是阅读指南——题材类型错位。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判要双要素并列，Illiberal Education and \"The Heart of the Matter\" 是四个选项中唯一同时点出核心诊断与评论对象、且无方向偏差的，自然锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"the illiberal nature of liberal education at our leading colleges and universities","opt":"Illiberal Education and \"The Heart of the Matter\""},{"orig":"its report may well set back reform by obscuring the depth and breadth of the challenge","opt":"Illiberal Education and \"The Heart of the Matter\""}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"The AAAS's Contribution to Liberal Education 把文章定调为对 AAAS 贡献的肯定颂扬，但作者的核心立场是批评 AAAS 报告未切中要害（参见 its report may well set back reform），方向颠倒。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Progressive Policy vs. Liberal Education 只对应 P5 中进步派思想与古典自由派思想的对照，遗漏 P1/P4/P6 评论 AAAS 报告的主线——把支撑段当主旨。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"ordering","title":"Section II Part B 段落排序","directions":"Directions: The following paragraphs are given in a wrong order. For questions 41 -45, you are required to reorganize these paragraphs into a coherent text by choosing from the list A-G and filling them into the numbered boxes. Paragraphs A and E have been correctly placed. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)","points":10,"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","label":"A","text":"Some archaeological sites have always been easily observable – for example, the Parthenon in Athens, Greece; the pyramids of Giza in Egypt; and the megaliths of Stonehenge in southern England. But these sites are exceptions to the norm. Most archaeological sites have been located by means of careful searching, while many others have been discovered by accident. Olduvai Gorge, an early hominid site in Tanzania, was found by a butterfly hunter who literally fell into its deep valley in 1911. Thousands of Aztec artifacts came to light during the digging of the Mexico City subway in the 1970s."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","label":"B","text":"In another case, American archaeologists René Million and George Cowgill spent years systematically mapping the entire city of Teotihuacán in the Valley of Mexico near what is now Mexico City. At its peak around AD 600, this city was one of the largest human settlements in the world. The researchers mapped not only the city's vast and ornate ceremonial areas, but also hundreds of simpler apartment complexes where common people lived."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","label":"C","text":"How do archaeologists know where to find what they are looking for when there is nothing visible on the surface of the ground? Typically, they survey and sample (make test excavations on) large areas of terrain to determine where excavation will yield useful information. Surveys and test samples have also become important for understanding the larger landscapes that contain archaeological sites."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","label":"D","text":"Surveys can cover a single large settlement or entire landscapes. In one case, many researchers working around the ancient Maya city of Copán, Honduras, have located hundreds of small rural villages and individual dwellings by using aerial photographs and by making surveys on foot. The resulting settlement maps show how the distribution and density of the rural population around the city changed dramatically between AD 500 and 850, when Copán collapsed."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","label":"E","text":"To find their sites, archaeologists today rely heavily on systematic survey methods and a variety of high-technology tools and techniques. Airborne technologies, such as different types of radar and photographic equipment carried by airplanes or spacecraft, allow archaeologists to learn about what lies beneath the ground without digging. Aerial surveys locate general areas of interest or larger buried features, such as ancient buildings or fields."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","label":"F","text":"Most archaeological sites, however, are discovered by archaeologists who have set out to look for them. Such searches can take years. British archaeologist Howard Carter knew that the tomb of the Egyptian pharaoh Tutankhamun existed from information found in other sites. Carter sifted through rubble in the Valley of the Kings for seven years before he located the tomb in 1922. In the late 1800s British archaeologist Sir Arthur Evans combed antique dealers' stores in Athens, Greece. He was searching for tiny engraved seals attributed to the ancient Mycenaean culture that dominated Greece from the 1400s to 1200s BC. Evans's interpretations of these engravings eventually led him to find the Minoan palace at Knossos (Knosós), on the island of Crete, in 1900."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-7","label":"G","text":"Ground surveys allow archaeologists to pinpoint the places where digs will be successful. Most ground surveys involve a lot of walking, looking for surface clues such as small fragments of pottery. They often include a certain amount of digging to test for buried materials at selected points across a landscape. Archaeologists also may locate buried remains by using such technologies as ground radar, magnetic-field recording, and metal detectors. Archaeologists commonly use computers to map sites and the landscapes around sites. Two- and three-dimensional maps are helpful tools in planning excavations, illustrating how sites look, and presenting the results of archaeological research."}],"choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Some archaeological sites have always been easily observable – for example, the Parthenon in Athens, Greece; the pyramids of Giza in Egypt; and the megaliths of Stonehenge in southern England. But these sites are exceptions to the norm. Most archaeological sites have been located by means of careful searching, while many others have been discovered by accident. Olduvai Gorge, an early hominid site in Tanzania, was found by a butterfly hunter who literally fell into its deep valley in 1911. Thousands of Aztec artifacts came to light during the digging of the Mexico City subway in the 1970s."},{"key":"B","text":"In another case, American archaeologists René Million and George Cowgill spent years systematically mapping the entire city of Teotihuacán in the Valley of Mexico near what is now Mexico City. At its peak around AD 600, this city was one of the largest human settlements in the world. The researchers mapped not only the city's vast and ornate ceremonial areas, but also hundreds of simpler apartment complexes where common people lived."},{"key":"C","text":"How do archaeologists know where to find what they are looking for when there is nothing visible on the surface of the ground? Typically, they survey and sample (make test excavations on) large areas of terrain to determine where excavation will yield useful information. Surveys and test samples have also become important for understanding the larger landscapes that contain archaeological sites."},{"key":"D","text":"Surveys can cover a single large settlement or entire landscapes. In one case, many researchers working around the ancient Maya city of Copán, Honduras, have located hundreds of small rural villages and individual dwellings by using aerial photographs and by making surveys on foot. The resulting settlement maps show how the distribution and density of the rural population around the city changed dramatically between AD 500 and 850, when Copán collapsed."},{"key":"E","text":"To find their sites, archaeologists today rely heavily on systematic survey methods and a variety of high-technology tools and techniques. Airborne technologies, such as different types of radar and photographic equipment carried by airplanes or spacecraft, allow archaeologists to learn about what lies beneath the ground without digging. Aerial surveys locate general areas of interest or larger buried features, such as ancient buildings or fields."},{"key":"F","text":"Most archaeological sites, however, are discovered by archaeologists who have set out to look for them. Such searches can take years. British archaeologist Howard Carter knew that the tomb of the Egyptian pharaoh Tutankhamun existed from information found in other sites. Carter sifted through rubble in the Valley of the Kings for seven years before he located the tomb in 1922. In the late 1800s British archaeologist Sir Arthur Evans combed antique dealers' stores in Athens, Greece. He was searching for tiny engraved seals attributed to the ancient Mycenaean culture that dominated Greece from the 1400s to 1200s BC. Evans's interpretations of these engravings eventually led him to find the Minoan palace at Knossos (Knosós), on the island of Crete, in 1900."},{"key":"G","text":"Ground surveys allow archaeologists to pinpoint the places where digs will be successful. Most ground surveys involve a lot of walking, looking for surface clues such as small fragments of pottery. They often include a certain amount of digging to test for buried materials at selected points across a landscape. Archaeologists also may locate buried remains by using such technologies as ground radar, magnetic-field recording, and metal detectors. Archaeologists commonly use computers to map sites and the landscapes around sites. Two- and three-dimensional maps are helpful tools in planning excavations, illustrating how sites look, and presenting the results of archaeological research."}],"questions":[{"n":41,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"C"},{"n":42,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"F"},{"n":43,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"G"},{"n":44,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"D"},{"n":45,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"B"}],"order":["C","A","F","E","G","D","B"],"fixed":{"1":"A","3":"E"},"chain":"41. → A → 42. → E → 43. → 44. → 45.","orderChain":"正确顺序 41 C → 预给 A → 42 F → 预给 E → 43 G → 44 D → 45 B","seams":["【承接前一段】 段 A 语义承接：A 说「多数遗址地表看不见、要靠搜寻」，C 顺势追问「看不见时怎么找」，问题正对接（弱锚，靠逻辑） 。41 紧贴 given 的 A。A 段尾落在「靠搜寻或偶然发现」、且整段都在讲遗址多半地表无明显痕迹；C 段首的设问 there is nothing visible on the surface of the ground 正是接着这个「看不见」往下问「那究竟怎么找」。无显式回指词，是语义承接，但方向唯一。","【引出后一段】 段 E 语义承接：F 讲完早年人工苦寻的案例，E 以 today + high-technology 把话题推到现代技术，时间与方法上正好递进 。42 夹在 C 与 given 的 E 之间。F 全段是人工搜寻的旧例（Carter 1922、Evans 1900），E 段首 archaeologists today rely heavily on ... high-technology tools 用 today 与「高科技」与之形成「过去靠苦寻 → 今天靠技术」的递进，F 在前、E 在后顺理成章。","【承接前一段】 段 E 词汇复现：E 段尾讲 Aerial surveys（空中），G 段首讲 Ground surveys（地面），是同一组对举词，紧贴相接 。43 紧跟 given 的 E。E 只讲了空中遥感这一类，段尾停在 Aerial surveys；G 段首 Ground surveys 正好补上地面这一类，Aerial 与 Ground 成对、且 surveys 一词复现，接缝最硬。","【承接前一段】 段 G 词汇复现：G 讲完地面勘查方法并落到地图工具，D 复现 Surveys 并转入「勘查能覆盖多大范围」的案例展开 。44 紧跟刚定下的 G。G 段尾讲到 Two- and three-dimensional maps are helpful tools in planning excavations（测绘成果），D 段首 Surveys can cover a single large settlement or entire landscapes. 顺势把 survey 从方法推进到「覆盖范围」的实例（Copán），Surveys 一词复现衔接。","【引出后一段】 段 B 逻辑连接词：D 用 In one case 开第一个案例，B 用 In another case 接第二个，one→another 成对锁死先后 。D 段内 In one case 是第一个案例（Copán），B 段首 In another case 是第二个案例（Teotihuacán）。one case 必在 another case 之前，所以 D 在 B 前，这条接缝同时帮 44、45 两位定锚。","【承接前一段】 段 D 逻辑连接词：B 段首 In another case 直接承接 D 的 In one case，是 one→another 配对的后半 。45 收尾。D 已用 In one case 给出 Copán 这第一个案例，B 段首 In another case 接出 Teotihuacán 这第二个案例，another 回指「前面已有一个 case」，唯一能对上的就是 D。B 段尾收束于测绘成果、不再引出新内容，正合末段。"]},{"id":"section2-part-c","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-c-1","text":"Music means different things to different people and sometimes even different things to the same person at different moments of his life. It might be poetic, philosophical, sensual, or mathematical, but in any case it must, in my view, have something to do with the soul of the human being. Hence it is metaphysical; but the means of expression is purely and exclusively physical: sound. I believe it is precisely this permanent coexistence of metaphysical message through physical means that is the strength of music. (46) It is also the reason why when we try to describe music with words, all we can do is articulate our reactions to it, and not grasp music itself."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-2","text":"Beethoven's importance in music has been principally defined by the revolutionary nature of his compositions. He freed music from hitherto prevailing conventions of harmony and structure. Sometimes I feel in his late works a will to break all signs of continuity. The music is abrupt and seemingly disconnected, as in the last piano sonata. In musical expression, he did not feel restrained by the weight of convention. (47) By all accounts he was a freethinking person, and a courageous one, and I find courage an essential quality for the understanding, let alone the performance, of his works."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-3","text":"This courageous attitude in fact becomes a requirement for the performers of Beethoven's music. His compositions demand the performer to show courage, for example in the use of dynamics. (48) Beethoven's habit of increasing the volume with an extreme intensity and then abruptly following it with a sudden soft passage was only rarely used by composers before him."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-4","text":"Beethoven was a deeply political man in the broadest sense of the word. He was not interested in daily politics, but concerned with questions of moral behavior and the larger questions of right and wrong affecting the entire society. (49) Especially significant was his view of freedom, which, for him, was associated with the rights and responsibilities of the individual: he advocated freedom of thought and of personal expression."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-5","text":"Beethoven's music tends to move from chaos to order as if order were an imperative of human existence. For him, order does not result from forgetting or ignoring the disorders that plague our existence; order is a necessary development, an improvement that may lead to the Greek ideal of spiritual elevation. It is not by chance that the Funeral March is not the last movement of the Eroica Symphony, but the second, so that suffering does not have the last word. (50) One could interpret much of the work of Beethoven by saying that suffering is inevitable, but the courage to fight it renders life worth living."}]},"sentences":[{"n":46,"en":"It is also the reason why when we try to describe music with words, all we can do is articulate our reactions to it, and not grasp music itself.","refZh":"这也正是为什么当我们试图用语言来描述音乐时，我们所能做的只是把自己对音乐的感受表达出来，而无法真正把握音乐本身。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"It is also the reason why","lit":"这也是……的原因","role":"（主干＋reason 的同位/定语从句引导）","note":"难点： It 回指还原＋why 引出原因从句 It 不是\"它\"，要还原成前句\"形而上内涵与物质声音并存\"这件事 this permanent coexistence of metaphysical message through physical means；why 在此引导一个长定语从句，修饰 reason，意为\"……之所以如此的原因\"，后面整段都在说\"什么的原因\"。"},{"en":"when we try to describe music with words,","lit":"当我们试图用语言描述音乐时","role":"（时间状语从句）","note":"难点： describe...with words＝\"用言语描述\" with words 是\"用文字/语言\"作方式状语，不要漏译；这是承接全文\"音乐之内涵难以言传\"的关键，译\"用语言/文字去描述音乐\"。"},{"en":"all we can do is articulate our reactions to it,","lit":"我们能做的全部就是表达我们对它的反应","role":"（主句（reason why 所修饰的内容））","note":"难点： all we can do is (to) do＝\"所能做的不过是\"；articulate＝清晰说出 all we can do is + 动词原形，是\"我们所能做的不过是……\"的固定结构，含\"仅此而已\"的限定意味。articulate 在此非\"灵活的\"，而是动词\"清楚地表达、说出\"（熟词僻义）。to it 的 it 指 music。"},{"en":"and not grasp music itself.","lit":"而无法把握音乐本身","role":"（并列谓语（与 articulate 并列，受 all we can do is 统辖））","note":"难点： grasp＝\"把握、领会\"（非\"抓住\"）；and not 表转折性对照 grasp 此处取抽象义\"领会、把握住\"，不译\"抓住\"。and not 与前面 articulate 形成对照：我们\"只能说出反应\"，\"却无法把握音乐本身\"，music itself 强调\"音乐本身\"。"}]},{"n":47,"en":"By all accounts he was a freethinking person, and a courageous one, and I find courage an essential quality for the understanding, let alone the performance, of his works.","refZh":"据大家所说，他是一个思想自由的人，也是一个勇敢的人；而我认为，勇气是理解他的作品所必不可少的一种品质，更不用说演奏他的作品了。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"By all accounts he was a freethinking person, and a courageous one,","lit":"据各方所说，他是一个思想自由的人，也是一个勇敢的人","role":"（第一分句（含并列表语））","note":"难点： By all accounts＝\"据大家所说/普遍认为\"；one 替代 person By all accounts 是固定短语，意为\"据各方/普遍说法\"，不是\"按所有账户\"。a courageous one 的 one 代替前面的 person，译\"一个勇敢的人\"即可，不必重复\"人\"也行。freethinking＝思想自由的。"},{"en":"and I find courage an essential quality","lit":"而我发现勇气是一种必不可少的品质","role":"（第二分句主干（find + 宾语 + 宾补））","note":"难点： find sth + 名词＝\"认为某物是……\"（宾补结构） find courage an essential quality 是\"find＋宾语 courage＋宾补 an essential quality\"，意为\"认为勇气是一种……的品质\"，不是\"发现一种品质\"。essential＝必不可少的、至关重要的。"},{"en":"for the understanding, let alone the performance, of his works.","lit":"对于理解他的作品而言——更不用说演奏了","role":"（介词短语作定语＋插入语 let alone）","note":"难点： let alone＝\"更不用说\"（含递进否定）；the understanding...of his works 被插入语隔断 the understanding ... of his works 本是一个整体\"对他作品的理解\"，中间被 let alone the performance 这个插入语切开。let alone 意为\"更别提、更不用说\"，表程度递进：理解尚且需要勇气，演奏就更需要了。还原结构：courage 对\"理解他的作品\"是必需品质，\"更不用说演奏\"。"}]},{"n":48,"en":"Beethoven's habit of increasing the volume with an extreme intensity and then abruptly following it with a sudden soft passage was only rarely used by composers before him.","refZh":"贝多芬习惯于以极强的力度增大音量，随即又突然转入一个骤然轻柔的乐段，这种手法在他之前的作曲家中极少被采用。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Beethoven's habit of increasing the volume with an extreme intensity","lit":"贝多芬以极强的力度增大音量的习惯","role":"（主语核心＋of 后置定语（动名词1））","note":"难点： habit of doing 整个是主语；volume＝音量、intensity＝（力度）强度 这一长串到 was 之前都是主语：核心词 habit，后面 of increasing... 是动名词作定语说明\"什么习惯\"。volume 此处指\"音量\"（不是\"体积/卷\"），intensity 指演奏\"力度的强度\"，都是音乐语境取义。"},{"en":"and then abruptly following it with a sudden soft passage","lit":"然后又突然接以一个骤然轻柔的乐段","role":"（of 后置定语的并列部分（动名词2））","note":"难点： following it 的 it 指前面增大的音量/强音；passage＝（乐曲的）乐段；soft＝（声音）轻柔 and then ... following 与前面 increasing 并列，同受 habit of 统辖，描述习惯的第二个动作。it 回指前句\"被增强的音量/强音\"。passage 在音乐语境是\"乐段、段落\"，不是\"通道\"；soft 指声音\"柔和、轻\"，不是\"软\"。abruptly／sudden 都强调\"突然\"。"},{"en":"was only rarely used by composers before him.","lit":"在他之前很少被作曲家使用","role":"（谓语（被动语态）＋时间/范围状语）","note":"难点： 被动 was used by＝\"被……使用\"，宜转主动；before him＝在他之前 was only rarely used by composers before him 是被动语态，汉语顺译\"被……\"略生硬，可转主动\"他之前的作曲家很少使用\"。only rarely＝极少、难得，before him＝在贝多芬之前。"}]},{"n":49,"en":"Especially significant was his view of freedom, which, for him, was associated with the rights and responsibilities of the individual: he advocated freedom of thought and of personal expression.","refZh":"尤为重要的是他对自由的看法。对他而言，这种自由观与个人的权利和责任紧密相关：他主张思想自由和个人表达的自由。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Especially significant was his view of freedom,","lit":"尤为重要的是他对自由的看法","role":"（主句（表语前置的倒装））","note":"难点： 完全倒装：表语 Especially significant 提到句首，正常语序是 His view...was especially significant 本是 His view of freedom was especially significant，为强调把表语 Especially significant 提到了句首形成倒装。翻译时还原成正常语序：\"他对自由的看法尤为重要/意义重大\"。significant＝重要的、有意义的。"},{"en":"which, for him, was associated with the rights and responsibilities of the individual:","lit":"对他而言，这种看法与个人的权利和责任相关联","role":"（which 引导的非限制性定语从句（含插入语 for him））","note":"难点： which 指 his view of freedom；for him 是插入语；be associated with＝\"与……相关联\" which 引导非限制性定语从句，先行词是 his view of freedom（他的自由观）。for him 被两个逗号夹着，是插入语\"对他来说\"，可单独提出。be associated with＝\"与……相联系、相关联\"。the individual＝个人、个体。"},{"en":"he advocated freedom of thought and of personal expression.","lit":"他主张思想自由和个人表达的自由","role":"（冒号后的解释说明（对上句的具体化））","note":"难点： advocate＝主张、提倡；freedom of thought and of personal expression＝两种自由并列 冒号在此引出对前文\"自由观\"的具体解释。advocate＝公开主张、倡导。freedom of thought and of personal expression 是 freedom of A and (freedom) of B 的省略，即\"思想自由\"与\"个人表达的自由\"两项并列。"}]},{"n":50,"en":"One could interpret much of the work of Beethoven by saying that suffering is inevitable, but the courage to fight it renders life worth living.","refZh":"人们可以这样解读贝多芬的大部分作品：苦难是不可避免的，但与苦难抗争的勇气却使生命变得值得度过。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"One could interpret much of the work of Beethoven by saying that","lit":"人们可以这样解读贝多芬的大部分作品，即……","role":"（主句（One 泛指主语）＋ by doing 方式状语）","note":"难点： One＝泛指\"人们\"；by saying that＝\"通过说……来（解读）\"引出宾语从句 One 不是\"一个人\"，而是泛指\"人们/我们\"。interpret＝解读、诠释。by saying that... 是方式状语\"通过这样说……\"，that 引出后面两个并列分句的内容，译时可处理成\"可以这样解读……即……\"。"},{"en":"suffering is inevitable,","lit":"苦难是不可避免的","role":"（saying 的宾语从句之一）","note":"难点： suffering＝苦难、苦痛；inevitable＝不可避免的 suffering 取名词\"苦难、痛苦\"，呼应全文\"贝多芬音乐从混乱走向秩序、苦难不是终曲\"的语境 suffering does not have the last word。inevitable＝必然的、不可避免的。"},{"en":"but the courage to fight it renders life worth living.","lit":"但与之抗争的勇气使生命值得一过","role":"（but 引导的并列转折分句（宾语从句之二））","note":"难点： it 指 suffering；render sth + 形容词＝\"使某物变得……\"；worth living＝值得活 to fight it 的 it 回指前句 suffering（苦难），即\"与苦难抗争的勇气\"。render 此处不是\"给予/呈现\"，而是\"使……变得\"（render＋宾语＋形容词，熟词僻义）。renders life worth living＝\"使生活变得值得（去）过\"，worth＋doing 表\"值得做\"。"}]}]},{"id":"section3-part-a","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part A 写作","directions":"51. Directions: Write a letter of about 100 words to the president of your university, suggesting how to improve students’ physical condition. You should include the details you think necessary. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter, use “Li Ming ” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","prompt":"51. Directions: Write a letter of about 100 words to the president of your university, suggesting how to improve students’ physical condition. You should include the details you think necessary. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter, use “Li Ming ” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","points":10,"image":null,"model":{"essay":"Dear President, I am a student from the Department of English. I am writing to offer some suggestions on how to improve students' physical condition. To begin with, I would suggest that the university build more sports facilities, such as basketball courts and a swimming pool, so that students have places to exercise. In addition, it would be advisable to organize regular sports activities, like a monthly running competition, to arouse students' interest. Above all, please ensure that everyone enjoys at least one free hour for exercise each day. I sincerely hope these suggestions will be taken into consideration. Thank you for your time. Yours sincerely, Li Ming","translation":"尊敬的校长：\n我是英语系的一名学生。我写信是想就如何改善学生的身体状况提出几点建议。\n首先，我建议学校增建更多体育设施，比如篮球场和一个游泳池，让学生有地方锻炼。此外，定期组织体育活动也很可取，比如每月一次的长跑比赛，以激发学生的兴趣。最重要的是，请保证每人每天至少有一小时的自由锻炼时间。\n我真诚地希望这些建议能被采纳。感谢您抽出时间。\n此致敬礼 李明","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"身份＋目的一句到位","text":"【第 1 段】 身份＋目的一句到位 。用 I am a student from the Department of English 自报身份，再用 I am writing to offer some suggestions 直接亮出来信目的，落实了首段‘称呼开门见山亮目的’的方法，让校长立刻明白信的用意。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"三条措施各配细节","text":"【第 2 段】 三条措施各配细节 。To begin with / In addition / Above all 领起三条措施，分别配上 basketball courts and a swimming pool、a monthly running competition、one free hour for exercise each day 三个细节，落实‘措施加细节各成一句’，把要求里的必要细节写实，措施不落空。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"谦逊收尾＋规范落款","text":"【第 3 段】 谦逊收尾＋规范落款 。I sincerely hope these suggestions will be taken into consideration 表达期望、Thank you for your time 致谢，末尾 Yours sincerely 后落款 Li Ming、通篇不写地址，落实‘礼貌收尾接落款’与署名硬要求。"}],"wordCount":108}},{"id":"section3-part-b","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part B 写作","directions":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following drawing. In your essay, you should 1)describe the drawing briefly, 2)interpret its intended meaning, and 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","prompt":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following drawing. In your essay, you should 1)describe the drawing briefly, 2)interpret its intended meaning, and 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2014-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg","alt":"这是一幅标题为“相携”的漫画，分为左右两部分","width":"1093","height":"651","local":"assets/writing/2014-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"The two pictures presented above vividly depict a touching scene of mutual care across generations. In the left one, captioned \"Thirty Years Ago\", a young mother holds her little daughter's hand as they walk together. In the right one, labelled \"Now\", that grown-up daughter tenderly supports her aged mother by the arm, and the whole cartoon carries the title \"Walking Hand in Hand\". Simple as it is, the drawing conveys a profound message about love flowing between family members. Decades ago the mother nurtured her helpless child; today the child, now an adult, returns that devotion by caring for her frail parent. Symbolically, it reveals how care and gratitude are passed on in a family, and how filial duty repays parental love. In my view, this cycle of affection is exactly what holds a family and a society together. As the pace of modern life quickens, some young people neglect their ageing parents, leaving them lonely. Therefore, we should follow the example in the picture: repay our parents with patience and company while there is still time. Only in this way can the warmth of walking hand in hand be carried from one generation to the next.","translation":"上面两幅图生动地描绘了一幕跨越两代人的相互关爱的温情画面。左图题为“三十年前”，一位年轻的母亲牵着小女儿的手一起走路；右图题为“现在”，那个已长大成人的女儿轻柔地搀扶着年迈母亲的手臂，整幅漫画取名为“相携”。\n画面虽简单，却传递出一个关于亲人之间爱意流动的深刻寓意。几十年前母亲养育无助的孩子；今天已长大成人的孩子以照料体弱母亲的方式回报这份深情。它象征性地揭示了关爱与感恩如何在一个家庭中代代相传，孝道又如何回报父母之爱。\n在我看来，这种爱的轮回正是维系家庭与社会的纽带。随着现代生活节奏加快，一些年轻人忽视了年迈的父母，让他们倍感孤独。因此，我们应当效仿画中的做法：趁着还来得及，用耐心和陪伴回报父母。唯有如此，“相携”的温暖才能一代代传递下去。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"总起加分述完成描述","text":"【第 1 段】 总起加分述完成描述 。首句 The two pictures presented above vividly depict... 用『总起描述』句架总领，随后 In the left one... / In the right one... 分述两图人物动作，只抓母牵女、女扶母与标题，未堆衣着细节，简洁落实了描述任务。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"过渡加对比点破寓意","text":"【第 2 段】 过渡加对比点破寓意 。Simple as it is 一句先搭桥过渡，再用 Decades ago... / today... 古今对比，最后 Symbolically, it reveals... 明确点破亲情反哺与孝道传承，紧扣画面而不跑题。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"态度加对策首尾呼应","text":"【第 3 段】 态度加对策首尾呼应 。In my view 亮明态度，随后联系 some young people neglect their ageing parents 的现实问题，用 Therefore, we should... 给出对策，结尾 walking hand in hand 回扣画作标题，实现首尾呼应与升华。"}],"wordCount":197}}],"questionCount":45,"objectiveCount":45,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 D where · 2 A fades · 3 B While · 4 A damaging · 5 C wellbeing · 6 D turns · 7 C workouts · 8 D functions · 9 B process · 10 C excel · 11 A However · 12 A according to · 13 B further · 14 D sharpness · 15 C allows · 16 B track · 17 A on · 18 B constantly · 19 C build · 20 D effective \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 A · 22 C · 23 D · 24 A · 25 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 D · 27 D · 28 A · 29 B · 30 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 B · 32 C · 33 C · 34 B · 35 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 A · 37 D · 38 C · 39 C · 40 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"段落排序 Section II Part B 41=C → 预给A → 42=F → 预给E → 43=G → 44=D → 45=B \n（逐题解析见 段落排序解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-c":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part C \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3-part-a":"写作 Section III Part A \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页","ans-section3-part-b":"写作 Section III Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":45,"explained":40,"missingSections":[]}};
